{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791666564,"nonce":"YZ1wMqxinWVYstFy4ZVLNq86Avg=","title":"Windows answers every font weight with the regular face","message":"CI run 38077152928 failed on windows-latest only: `binding::tests::bound_text_style::a_bound_weight_is_measured_at_that_weight` (\"black measured no wider than regular: 87\"). It passes on macOS and Linux and passed on Windows at c6e9019f.\n\nCause: `FontRegistry::new` preloads `KNOWN_FONT_PATHS`, and on Windows that list held only regular files (segoeui, consola, arial, times, cour). Each weight and italic is a separate file there. A styled lookup queries fontdb among the faces already loaded and takes the nearest, so weight 900 resolved to Segoe UI Regular; the full system scan only runs when a lookup finds nothing. Linux and Android list their Bold files and macOS preloads Helvetica.ttc (with bold) and the variable SF, which is why they pass.\n\nThe test started failing with 3884d665950425d4e3f1c46b1e384051ad86d77e (b43626b), when the measurer began resolving faces through `resolve_styled`. Before that it used cached faces only, missed in a fresh process, and fell back to the character estimate, which widens heavy weights. The renderer resolves faces the same way, so Windows apps drew bold and black text in the regular face whenever nothing had triggered the full system scan.\n\nFix: list Segoe UI Semibold, Bold, Black, Italic and Bold Italic, and Consolas, Arial and Times Bold, on Windows. Missing files are skipped.\n\nNot done: a lookup that only finds a distant weight among the preloaded faces could trigger the system scan instead, which would cover fonts no list names. That changes resolution on every platform, macOS's variable SF included, so it is left for a separate change.","files":null}]}